    {
      "type": "reflect",
      "kicker": "Tell me what you know",
      "prompt": "What’s the difference between an observation, an interpretation and an unsupported claim?",
      "modelAnswer": "An observation is something I can point at on the chart, like a close. An interpretation is a reasonable, hedged read of that evidence, like “buyers appear more aggressive.” An unsupported claim names who, why or what will happen, and the chart can’t prove it."
